# Pivot Navigation Comes On With Minimal UI

Turning **Pivot Navigation** on always turns **Minimal UI** on with it.
Turning **Minimal UI** on always pivots the nav to the horizontal top bar.
The two Appearance rows come on as a pair. Off stays independent — the
chevron can still expand the bar without leaving pivot.

## What this means on the surface

- Toggle Pivot Navigation on → the nav becomes a horizontal top bar of
  logo, Appearance, and you (Minimal UI).
- Toggle Minimal UI on → same top bar, not a vertical logo strip.
- Toggle either off on its own → the other stays as it was.
- The chevron beside the logo still reveals the full nav (Minimal UI off)
  while the bar stays pivoted.

## How it is wired

`setMenuPivot(true)` in `js/agent-menu.js` applies Minimal UI and stands
down Nav & History icons (that mode hides the Minimal UI strip). The
Appearance Minimal UI row in `js/appearance-menu.js` calls `setMenuPivot(true)`
when turning on. First paint (`js/text-size-fouc.js`) and
`restoreMinimalUi()` honor a stored pivot so the four-icon rail cannot
flash over the strip.

## Rules for the agent

- Never turn Pivot on without also turning Minimal UI on.
- Never turn Minimal UI on from Appearance without also pivoting.
- Do not force them off together — expand-via-chevron and a solo off
  must keep working.
- Do not reintroduce a path that paints Nav & History icons over a
  pivoted Minimal UI bar on load.
